## BACKGROUND SERVICE WORKER (service-worker.js)

Handles:
- Message routing between content scripts and popup
- All AI API calls (never call AI from content scripts)
- License validation
- PDF generation trigger via offscreen document
- Application count tracking

### Message types to handle:

```js
// From content scripts:
{ type: "JOB_DETECTED", payload: { platform, jobTitle, company, jobDescription, url, screeningQuestions } }

// From popup:
{ type: "GENERATE_APPLICATION", payload: { jobData, cvText, userProfile, preferences } }
{ type: "VALIDATE_LICENSE", payload: { key } }
{ type: "GENERATE_PDF", payload: { cvText, template } }
{ type: "GET_APPLICATION_COUNT" }

// To popup:
{ type: "APPLICATION_READY", payload: { tailoredCV, coverLetter, screeningAnswers, matchScore } }
{ type: "JOB_DETECTED", payload: { ... } }  // Forward to popup to trigger review panel
```

### AI call flow:

```js
async function generateApplication(jobData, cvText, userProfile, preferences) {
  const { provider, apiKey, model } = await getAIConfig();

  const systemPrompt = PROMPTS.system(userProfile);
  const userPrompt = PROMPTS.generateApplication(cvText, jobData, preferences);

  // Call AI (see ai.js)
  const result = await callAI({ provider, apiKey, model, systemPrompt, userPrompt });

  // Parse structured JSON response
  return parseApplicationResponse(result);
}
```

