## CONTENT SCRIPTS

### detector.js (shared)

Runs on all supported pages. Detects the platform and job listing, then dynamically injects the appropriate platform script.

```js
// Detect platform from URL and page structure
// Send JOB_DETECTED message to background service worker
// Only fire once per page load
// Do NOT auto-fill anything — only scrape and report
```

### greenhouse.js

Scrapes:
- Job title: `h1.app-title`
- Company: from page title or meta
- Job description: `#content .job-description` (inner text)
- Screening questions: `label` elements associated with form inputs

Fills (after FILL_FORM message received from background):
- Name, email, phone: standard input fields
- CV upload: generate PDF blob, create File object, trigger file input
- Cover letter: textarea
- Screening questions: match label text to answer, fill inputs/selects
- Use humanise.js for all interactions

### linkedin.js

LinkedIn Easy Apply uses a multi-step modal. Strategy:
- Detect Easy Apply button: `button.jobs-apply-button`
- Do NOT click it automatically — wait for user approval
- After approval, click Easy Apply, then fill each modal step
- Steps are identified by progress indicator
- Handle: text inputs, dropdowns, radio buttons, file upload, textarea
- If an unknown question type is encountered: pause, message popup to ask user

### indeed.js

Indeed has two apply flows:
1. Native Indeed apply — handle like Greenhouse
2. "Apply on company site" redirect — detect this and inform user in popup that the role redirects externally (do not attempt to fill)

