## POPUP UI

Built with React 18 + Vite. Four views:

### Dashboard.jsx
- Shows current page detection status: "Greenhouse job detected: Senior Frontend Engineer at Acme Corp"
- Match score badge if already generated
- "Review Application" CTA button
- Quick stats: applications this week, response rate

### ReviewPanel.jsx
- Two-column layout: left = tailored CV, right = cover letter
- Both are editable textareas (user can tweak before approving)
- Match score prominently displayed with rationale
- Screening Q&A list (editable)
- Three actions: **Approve & Fill** | **Regenerate** | **Skip**
- If daily limit approaching: warning banner

### ApplicationTracker.jsx
- Table: Company | Role | Date | Platform | Match Score | Status
- Status is a dropdown (applied/interview/rejected/offer/withdrawn)
- Click row to expand: shows CV snapshot, cover letter, screening answers
- Export to CSV button

### Settings.jsx
Sections:
1. **API Key** — provider toggle (Anthropic/OpenAI), key input (masked), test button
2. **Your CV** — paste CV text or upload PDF (parsed to text client-side via pdf.js)
3. **Profile** — all user_profile fields
4. **Preferences** — cover letter mode, auto-submit toggle, daily limit, CV template
5. **License** — current tier, applications used, upgrade CTA / license key input

### LicenseGate.jsx
- Shown when free tier limit (15 applications) is reached
- Clean paywall: "You've used your 15 free applications"
- "Upgrade to Pro — £8/mo or £49/year" button → opens LemonSqueezy checkout in new tab
- "Already have a license key?" input field

