## CODING STANDARDS

- Use ES modules throughout (type: "module" in service worker)
- React 18 functional components only, hooks-based state
- No class components
- Tailwind CSS for popup UI
- All storage access via the `storage.js` helper (never raw chrome.storage calls in components)
- All DB access via `db.js` (never raw IndexedDB calls in components)
- Content scripts must be side-effect free on load — only activate after JOB_DETECTED confirmation
- Never console.log API keys, CV text, or personal data
- All AI calls go through background service worker only — never from content scripts or popup directly

---

## KNOWN GOTCHAS

1. **MV3 service worker lifecycle** — service workers terminate after ~30s of inactivity. Use `chrome.storage` to persist state, not in-memory variables.
2. **Offscreen document** — only one can exist at a time. Check `chrome.offscreen.hasDocument()` before creating.
3. **LinkedIn DOM** — uses React internally, so standard input value setting won't trigger React's state. Use `Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(window.HTMLInputElement.prototype, 'value').set.call(input, value)` then dispatch an `input` event.
4. **Greenhouse file upload** — use `DataTransfer` API to programmatically set file input value.
5. **Content Security Policy** — extension popup cannot make fetch calls to external APIs in some configurations. Route all external calls through background service worker via `chrome.runtime.sendMessage`.
6. **jsPDF in offscreen** — import via CDN in offscreen.html, not as npm module, to avoid bundling issues.
